After the snowfall and the subsequent drop in temperatures, some terraces could also be covered in icing.
In some places drivers will encounter fog, but the visibility will gradually improve.
This can be seen from the reports of the road operations control centre in the region.
The D5 motorway is almost unrestricted, although it is recommended to exercise extreme caution, especially on the road between kilometer 80 and 131.
The surface of most first-class roads is iced and ice-free.
In the Pilsen and Tachov road area bordering Germany there can be stretches with ice sheets.
The second- and third-rate tracks are wet, so, in this case, there is also warning of stretches with icing plates.
Drivers should be wiser, especially on less-trapped tracks in the Eumava area.
